# Geometric points and their étale neighborhoods

A geometric point of a scheme `S` is a morphism `Spec k ⟶ S` with `k` algebraically closed, and
an étale neighborhood of one is an étale scheme over `S` carrying a lift of it. Parts (1)--(4) of
Stacks 03PO are stated in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.EtaleCohomology.NeighborhoodsStalksPoints.Basic`, as
`AlgebraicGeometry.GeometricPoint`, `AlgebraicGeometry.GeometricPoint.LiesOver`,
`AlgebraicGeometry.GeometricPoint.EtaleNeighborhood` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.GeometricPoint.EtaleNeighborhood.Hom`, and are re-exported here.

